\begin{proof}
	Given any $g\in (\Sigma_{\inn}^d)^R$, we can use \cref{thm:ael_decoding_technical} with radius $\beta = \delta_{\inn} - 2\eps$ to recover the list $\calL(g,\beta) = \{h\in \AELC ~\vert~ \Delta_R(g,h) \leq \beta\}$, as long as the following conditions are met:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item The list size for $\calC_{\inn}$ is constant at $\beta+\eps = \delta_{\inn}-\eps$, which is true by our choice of $\calC_{\inn}$.
		\item The outer code can be unique decoded up to a radius $\delta_{\dec}$, which is true by assumption.
		\item $\lambda \leq \gamma$ for $\gamma = \frac{\eps \cdot \delta_{\dec}}{4K}$, which is true by our choice of $\lambda$. 
	\end{itemize}
	To analyze the runtime, we note that the time needed to list decode $\calC_{\inn}$ from radius $\beta+\eps$, $\tlocal{\beta+\eps}$, is at most $|\Sigma_{\inn}|^d$ by a brute force search. As long as $\lambda \leq \gamma^2/2500$, which holds by our choice of $\lambda$, the time needed to compute an $(\eta,\gamma)$-regular family with $\gamma = \frac{\eps \cdot \delta_{\dec}}{4K}$ and $\eta = \Omega(\gamma^2)$ is $\treg{\gamma} = \Ot{nd}$.


The final runtime therefore is $n\cdot |\Sigma_{\inn}|^d+ K\cdot \Ot{nd} + T_{\dec}\cdot \exp(K^5/(\eps^3\cdot \delta_{\dec}^3))$.
\end{proof}
